  'Tourism Planning and Development',
  'A Year 3 core course in evidence-based, participatory, sustainable, and implementable destination planning. Students move from tourism-system diagnosis through stakeholder engagement, spatial and infrastructure planning, sustainability, culture, mobility, governance, economics, visitor management, climate resilience, data, and an integrated destination development plan.',
  $tpdvjson${"slug": "tourism-planning-and-development", "title": "Tourism Planning and Development", "description": "A Year 3 core course in evidence-based, participatory, sustainable, and implementable destination planning. Students move from tourism-system diagnosis through stakeholder engagement, spatial and infrastructure planning, sustainability, culture, mobility, governance, economics, visitor management, climate resilience, data, and an integrated destination development plan.", "topics": [{"id": "d5052703-1ce2-470a-a857-fd46fd902959", "type": "topic", "title": "Tourism Systems, Demand Drivers, and Futures", "description": "Frames tourism as an interconnected visitor economy shaped by markets, hosts, firms, infrastructure, institutions, technology, shocks, and environmental limits.", "children": [{"id": "3f93a280-487b-4884-b733-620f3d880c20", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The destination as a system", "children": [{"id": "a62319d5-6acd-4a3c-8104-f0024631d0b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Origins, destinations, transit routes, and gateways"}, {"id": "e4ae8df6-2adf-44cf-a388-4f4a507a80cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Visitors, residents, firms, workers, governments, and civil society"}, {"id": "4de9dfbf-bccf-4a5d-a3fa-1f836d2d6958", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply chains, services, attractions, and enabling infrastructure"}, {"id": "3771b718-fe12-4d15-afb6-7a3892cc43b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback loops, externalities, dependencies, and system boundaries"}], "description": "Systems thinking reveals how visitor demand, businesses, residents, infrastructure, ecosystems, and policy interact."}, {"id": "01536eb1-be16-41f8-b4de-b4e6eac96a92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand and market drivers", "children": [{"id": "de7d0169-75cc-4725-b269-dddd5b0aacdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Income, demographics, exchange rates, visas, and connectivity"}, {"id": "a24a4512-9bc5-499b-9e5e-32c3d62c03cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Motivations, segments, source markets, and trip purpose"}, {"id": "91dbce0a-0de1-45ec-8133-2fecc1e472a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonality, length of stay, spend, and repeat visitation"}, {"id": "dc358168-3fca-455d-bb26-361e5769fc63", "type": "concept", "title": "Technology, media, geopolitics, and consumer values"}], "description": "Planning must distinguish durable demand drivers from short-lived enthusiasm."}, {"id": "ab316502-a27b-49b9-becd-097181950c9b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forecasting and scenarios", "children": [{"id": "4a00fe71-35ab-4622-88d6-d6d8b4747d31", "type": "concept", "title": "Trend extrapolation and judgmental forecasts"}, {"id": "53e64a10-743f-4745-bad5-9c11d21620d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline, high/low, and shock scenarios"}, {"id": "e6155643-65cb-43fc-b3f1-37f6077a9adc", "type": "concept", "title": "Weak signals and critical uncertainties"}, {"id": "ebd71029-bdcd-48fe-8e34-68c5be4699e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Robust, adaptive, and trigger-based strategies"}], "description": "Alternative futures prevent a plan from depending on a single fragile forecast."}]}, {"id": "483d956e-5a04-40ae-b41a-8496794194f2", "type": "topic", "title": "Destination Evolution, Competitiveness, and Strategic Position", "description": "Uses life-cycle and competitiveness models to diagnose a destination's position, path dependencies, product portfolio, and strategic choices.", "children": [{"id": "ea0ccfdd-1061-412f-af06-729dfa62e137", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Destination life cycle", "children": [{"id": "51c13206-4da7-4c61-8743-fa0892e41538", "type": "concept", "title": "Exploration, involvement, development, consolidation, and stagnation"}, {"id": "db659c6a-58eb-4759-8bb1-617925ea0d0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Decline, stabilization, or rejuvenation pathways"}, {"id": "f1f2775c-8591-4999-8b31-0e0b3b124b32", "type": "concept", "title": "Indicators of phase and turning points"}, {"id": "46b4a33c-07fe-4ca4-8918-ddcfaafb1237", "type": "concept", "title": "Model limitations and path dependence"}], "description": "Life-cycle models help diagnose development pressures without assuming every destination follows the same path."}, {"id": "f54518e9-4e37-4e0b-b147-855476fcfce3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Competitiveness and comparative advantage", "children": [{"id": "e0a138ad-8ab5-4291-8aca-a5eb80689fe8", "type": "concept", "title": "Core resources and attractors"}, {"id": "b431d957-1ebb-414e-967b-8b62d74a1f8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Supporting factors and enabling conditions"}, {"id": "963306cc-e5f8-4aa8-8a93-1e8fe5e312f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Destination management and policy"}, {"id": "cb87e54d-7bcf-4e0d-b0c8-e5d11253b62b", "type": "concept", "title": "Price, quality, accessibility, reputation, and resilience"}], "description": "Competitiveness depends on converting resources into valued experiences while sustaining place quality."}, {"id": "a5a954ea-fa7d-4eb6-8c24-e3ed08d5cce5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio and strategic position", "children": [{"id": "776e4426-9dcb-4ad7-b454-3cb0cba077ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Product-market matrix and visitor segments"}, {"id": "c0059bf4-3455-4da2-9179-f8c181b2f0a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonal and geographic diversification"}, {"id": "7eb277eb-7e86-49f2-817d-761df051c723", "type": "concept", "title": "Clusters, routes, events, and signature experiences"}, {"id": "9d4f4eaa-5388-4326-984e-80fcf47fde70", "type": "concept", "title": "SWOT/TOWS, benchmarking, and strategic choice"}], "description": "A destination needs a coherent mix of markets, places, seasons, and experiences."}]}, {"id": "5d862159-4c4e-4797-989c-6d712625738e", "type": "topic", "title": "Tourism Impacts, Resident Well-Being, and Distribution", "description": "Assesses economic, social, cultural, and environmental effects, with attention to who benefits, who bears costs, and how residents experience change.", "children": [{"id": "791b1a63-f247-4e3f-80df-3f3fda764412", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic impacts", "children": [{"id": "23bfd873-0f9c-42cd-9ad6-4ac35259a98d", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct, indirect, and induced effects"}, {"id": "ded8357a-31c7-4eb9-b0f1-075d1fea7f8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Employment quality, wages, entrepreneurship, and tax revenue"}, {"id": "c73dac01-423a-4581-855e-01f7a6d3dc64", "type": "concept", "title": "Leakage, imports, displacement, and opportunity cost"}, {"id": "6186fb4d-f9b2-444c-951a-7fede73ff2d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Local linkages, multipliers, and distribution"}], "description": "Headline spending matters less than the net local value retained and distributed."}, {"id": "6e214d94-c7dc-475b-b6e9-fdd418a864ac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social and cultural impacts", "children": [{"id": "01b86353-604f-41f0-a882-ab4797a1d8be", "type": "concept", "title": "Housing, cost of living, public space, and services"}, {"id": "3e698cc5-aeb0-424f-89f1-b2954343eae5", "type": "concept", "title": "Crowding, behavior, safety, and community cohesion"}, {"id": "0ed99348-857a-4f45-a9e4-c7521707bfde", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodification, cultural change, and revitalization"}, {"id": "1a722dc9-dd60-404d-aec5-f3a31e60bc8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Resident attitudes, social exchange, and quality of life"}], "description": "Tourism reshapes everyday life, identity, access, and power as well as visitor experiences."}, {"id": "14156f73-9c1f-45d0-913b-6d33c48da429", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Environmental impacts", "children": [{"id": "a8e52905-4690-4528-8d8f-991c2c5fb248", "type": "concept", "title": "Water, energy, land, waste, and emissions"}, {"id": "80306f55-657f-4eeb-84c4-bbe904235c49", "type": "concept", "title": "Biodiversity, habitat, landscape, and noise"}, {"id": "35400e0f-397d-4fdc-9186-f794f7e1e78c", "type": "concept", "title": "Cumulative, seasonal, and induced effects"}, {"id": "5ddbd7ba-4082-4f99-9ff4-28af482d2fbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental justice and ecosystem services"}], "description": "Destination quality depends on managing resource use and cumulative ecological pressure."}]}, {"id": "7e0a6481-c944-4504-91f7-59367aac1797", "type": "topic", "title": "Community Participation, Stakeholders, and Social License", "description": "Builds legitimate planning processes through stakeholder mapping, inclusive engagement, conflict navigation, co-design, and accountable feedback.", "children": [{"id": "201d1a89-6957-4805-9af6-3cb171cc4d4c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stakeholder and power mapping", "children": [{"id": "9356ed89-2f22-4e6a-8d9f-3b6113083855", "type": "concept", "title": "Public, private, community, Indigenous, and civil-society actors"}, {"id": "884577c0-7049-47b9-9928-037795011a91", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest-influence and network maps"}, {"id": "460a1b7e-5b66-4ce0-bb32-e931e390f1a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Rights holders versus stakeholders"}, {"id": "4bdea01e-47b6-442c-8556-bb08b6ae8d0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Power asymmetry, gatekeepers, and missing voices"}], "description": "Participation is meaningful only when planners understand interests, influence, rights, and under-representation."}, {"id": "4039beff-cb36-4eef-ac83-a0eefcb5a598", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Engagement and co-design", "children": [{"id": "0ce6a9d6-8057-4cbb-94a4-c9a9a9a56e5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Information, consultation, involvement, collaboration, and empowerment"}, {"id": "fb0bb080-afe5-4e7e-86f0-9578e96f4907", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviews, workshops, charrettes, surveys, and deliberative forums"}, {"id": "b2864132-81df-4a20-aeb3-107592c1febc", "type": "concept", "title": "Language, access, compensation, timing, and digital inclusion"}, {"id": "485f9a1d-a77b-4ade-90d1-ae5f70c1ac2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Participatory visioning, mapping, and priority setting"}], "description": "Different planning decisions require different levels and methods of participation."}, {"id": "97e889aa-0ee8-4003-9092-f58f647a142d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict, trust, and accountability", "children": [{"id": "1316c82c-35b3-4722-9548-33f2e7bad605", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue framing and conflict diagnosis"}, {"id": "3b98b8bd-c619-44c1-aa13-8293d410a212", "type": "concept", "title": "Negotiation, mediation, and consensus limits"}, {"id": "d77be00c-a6e6-4037-aeea-1c4ee13045ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Grievance and appeal mechanisms"}, {"id": "76efad33-59f5-4d58-98ad-839acb50c41c", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision logs, feedback reports, and ongoing stewardship"}], "description": "Social license grows through transparent choices, visible tradeoffs, and credible response to feedback."}]}, {"id": "a3e01fe9-4e07-42f3-9e54-06c6a2be06d9", "type": "topic", "title": "Spatial Planning, Land Use, Infrastructure, and GIS", "description": "Connects tourism strategy to place through zoning, site selection, infrastructure capacity, environmental constraints, accessibility, mapping, and cumulative effects.", "children": [{"id": "bce84e78-35c9-4242-8b7d-0c18b963157a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory and spatial diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "6bf8b87c-fbe5-49bd-a65b-b7d131e7b06f", "type": "concept", "title": "Attractions, services, accommodation, communities, and infrastructure"}, {"id": "4fc744b0-655b-4d6b-af04-095d96c325c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitive ecosystems, hazards, heritage, and protected areas"}, {"id": "cc51be7e-1590-426f-ba94-f85cdf0647ce", "type": "concept", "title": "GIS layers, field audits, and participatory mapping"}, {"id": "713e54b6-bcf2-4f1f-b29b-3e6b31dbcc58", "type": "concept", "title": "Hot spots, gaps, clusters, and corridors"}], "description": "Mapping makes assets, constraints, access, and uneven impacts visible."}, {"id": "382f1630-55a6-4031-ace8-05a03ff2d132", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Land use and site planning", "children": [{"id": "62feda3d-fc32-474f-aed7-aa68d6658f53", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoning, overlays, setbacks, density, and design controls"}, {"id": "dcb8c387-903c-490b-a65c-eac2361278cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Site suitability and alternatives analysis"}, {"id": "f641a692-f70a-42ea-a822-87441f9d1305", "type": "concept", "title": "Landscape, public realm, and sense of place"}, {"id": "0f384eb9-b71d-43ca-8111-37754f19c36f", "type": "concept", "title": "Cumulative effects and induced development"}], "description": "Tourism projects must fit place capacity, regulation, and community goals."}, {"id": "478595bc-0c9e-43f8-a914-8a22db181b18", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infrastructure and service capacity", "children": [{"id": "66edc316-5581-4ab8-92fb-c4f9240016f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Water, wastewater, solid waste, energy, and digital connectivity"}, {"id": "44a2fdf8-3bf4-4110-a508-8d31a6e06a07", "type": "concept", "title": "Health, safety, emergency, and public-space capacity"}, {"id": "353b91e9-423d-4798-9896-fe55d25b2c18", "type": "concept", "title": "Phasing, thresholds, and capital planning"}, {"id": "226fd8e2-4519-4d9c-b9b0-27b9cdc59ee9", "type": "concept", "title": "Operations, maintenance, and lifecycle costs"}], "description": "Visitor growth is viable only when utilities and public services can perform without displacing resident needs."}]}, {"id": "befc3ed1-43d5-40e5-93fe-2c07f87c1ba1", "type": "topic", "title": "Sustainable and Regenerative Tourism", "description": "Moves beyond minimizing harm toward measurable destination stewardship, local value creation, ecosystem restoration, resource efficiency, and long-term resilience.", "children": [{"id": "df4361a0-c5f9-416e-9e30-bcf6970f0d62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sustainability frameworks", "children": [{"id": "92488f3c-9f44-4f11-8246-192f51cfd7ee", "type": "concept", "title": "GSTC Destination Criteria"}, {"id": "28e2e26b-914b-4b8e-b008-31a09e2c0dcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Sustainable Development Goals and policy alignment"}, {"id": "652efe32-c242-4805-a110-3a920a122404", "type": "concept", "title": "Materiality, boundaries, baselines, and targets"}, {"id": "95048581-199a-4008-b8c9-fd263ec5303c", "type": "concept", "title": "Certification, assurance, and greenwashing risk"}], "description": "Standards turn broad aspirations into auditable management, socioeconomic, cultural, and environmental commitments."}, {"id": "2c51f8cd-0b62-4842-b7cd-8052d402966d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resource efficiency and circularity", "children": [{"id": "54209cce-988b-42d7-ba52-abd4403a489c", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy efficiency and renewable supply"}, {"id": "d9a7f5ba-5f92-4ef0-a89c-7795e23d797c", "type": "concept", "title": "Water stewardship and wastewater reuse"}, {"id": "55d32c2b-e421-4685-aec8-95b33a7bdab7", "type": "concept", "title": "Waste prevention, food systems, and circular procurement"}, {"id": "3087b681-5a9f-4b14-85f3-000032321827", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-carbon construction and operations"}], "description": "Destinations can reduce cost and pressure by redesigning material and energy flows."}, {"id": "0e8e7e36-7722-4910-b9bd-f94d22c74562", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regeneration and stewardship", "children": [{"id": "278edbf2-5129-4090-b6b4-e6009586618a", "type": "concept", "title": "Nature-positive and restoration projects"}, {"id": "1b3a40be-07b2-4c4c-ae9f-b238c72da544", "type": "concept", "title": "Community wealth and local ownership"}, {"id": "88b68518-00fa-41bf-a1b3-1374fb169614", "type": "concept", "title": "Visitor contribution and stewardship programs"}, {"id": "4791b831-6049-454d-8605-38f271fa2b3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits, tradeoffs, and evidence of net benefit"}], "description": "Regenerative approaches ask how tourism can improve ecological and community capacity rather than merely reduce damage."}]}, {"id": "e72dbd86-918c-44d6-a78c-196a816d3f73", "type": "topic", "title": "Cultural, Heritage, and Indigenous Tourism", "description": "Plans visitor experiences that protect living culture and heritage, respect rights and ownership, and avoid extractive or inauthentic development.", "children": [{"id": "356d9002-e7bd-4386-93b4-169840d172d4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Heritage values and significance", "children": [{"id": "141af013-dc82-437a-ac07-1c8adc286bfa", "type": "concept", "title": "Tangible, intangible, natural, and living heritage"}, {"id": "ba630f98-9cb0-4789-9037-783cd22f4b1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Significance, authenticity, integrity, and change"}, {"id": "c42103f1-8dd6-4141-9aab-a608b5e14571", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural landscapes and memory"}, {"id": "de26d3d8-4181-40e4-8da0-06fb807a6594", "type": "concept", "title": "Heritage inventories and vulnerability"}], "description": "Planning begins with what communities value, not only what can be packaged for visitors."}, {"id": "d339d287-ad2c-42dc-9f19-5b14f29a4900", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rights, ownership, and representation", "children": [{"id": "52e057a0-9c39-4921-b81b-896beb8b1dd1", "type": "concept", "title": "Free, prior, and informed consent concepts"}, {"id": "593749bf-4cae-43c0-a006-d5d5f192f395", "type": "concept", "title": "Intellectual and cultural property"}, {"id": "c7e7be21-3d46-4450-924a-6a965294813b", "type": "concept", "title": "Community-led interpretation and protocols"}, {"id": "e5289580-9107-46b1-8be7-c74616eb8477", "type": "concept", "title": "Revenue sharing, employment, and ownership"}], "description": "Communities and Indigenous peoples must control how culture, stories, images, knowledge, and sacred places are used."}, {"id": "a0cf4728-9087-41e6-a9a3-e88bfd7c6f25", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visitor and site management", "children": [{"id": "b4792930-8746-45d8-a0bd-90fcd2ad945d", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretive planning and truthful narratives"}, {"id": "82b446a3-dc6f-4767-b2c2-03e3b17254f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, zoning, routes, timing, and behavior"}, {"id": "59aca6fd-e077-49d0-bdc7-98f7fc62bd55", "type": "concept", "title": "Conservation financing and reinvestment"}, {"id": "fe83e36b-3214-4b4a-85a0-5ad86042b0f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk from commodification, crowding, and staged authenticity"}], "description": "Interpretation and access should enrich understanding while protecting values and daily life."}]}, {"id": "2ab6b507-1dbb-4e69-b64c-6eee6683adcf", "type": "topic", "title": "Destination Organizations, Place Strategy, and Product Development", "description": "Clarifies the evolving role of DMOs/DMMOs in governance, research, product development, visitor management, partnerships, and responsible place communication.", "children": [{"id": "ef0b4ca0-707b-42f1-9b8f-f8682cddad2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "DMO/DMMO mandate and governance", "children": [{"id": "314e19c3-784f-4588-8891-53aafe222227", "type": "concept", "title": "Legal form, membership, board, and accountability"}, {"id": "7526a552-7004-40a8-b020-3e5e7b3ca604", "type": "concept", "title": "Public funding, levies, partnerships, and conflicts"}, {"id": "1677cc91-9364-4841-a94e-7feca48cc948", "type": "concept", "title": "Research, product, marketing, and visitor services"}, {"id": "7c96f984-6489-4543-850d-d6704da2b56c", "type": "concept", "title": "Resident engagement and destination stewardship"}], "description": "Destination organizations increasingly manage and steward places, not simply promote them."}, {"id": "9c5ebb5c-0b92-4daa-88d8-af1702429dfb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Place strategy and brand", "children": [{"id": "46d12426-3f50-4569-aefa-ecaf3735d8df", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity, positioning, value proposition, and narrative"}, {"id": "770d74eb-990d-498f-920b-f1fac471d232", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand architecture and portfolio"}, {"id": "00f99349-aa55-4165-8d57-34d1c949c5fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Market fit and ethical representation"}, {"id": "2dfc557d-f883-4ec3-9e71-90366af76a72", "type": "concept", "title": "Reputation, crisis communication, and brand governance"}], "description": "A credible place promise must emerge from distinctive assets and resident values, then align experience and communication."}, {"id": "2d180bc5-68aa-4b95-a4f6-4b70c64a6e5a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experience and product development", "children": [{"id": "4a77cef0-b5f4-4d8c-a896-0c68e122f163", "type": "concept", "title": "Experience design and visitor journeys"}, {"id": "02693ded-3ea3-4362-b802-f442d8246d74", "type": "concept", "title": "Routes, clusters, events, and thematic products"}, {"id": "9a6b7a26-1f06-4e09-b154-51c6a5f1ee0b", "type": "concept", "title": "SME capability, packaging, distribution, and quality"}, {"id": "c19f941c-cdb4-417e-a786-fcb147a4965d", "type": "concept", "title": "Prototyping, season extension, and market testing"}], "description": "Products combine places, services, stories, people, and operations into bookable, accessible experiences."}]}, {"id": "0f1d0d80-6097-42b5-af42-22da0f36adcb", "type": "topic", "title": "Transportation, Access, Mobility, and Visitor Flows", "description": "Integrates gateways, last-mile access, mobility networks, universal design, congestion, emissions, seasonality, and visitor-flow management.", "children": [{"id": "2e4da67f-764a-4688-9acf-8f81e93efbe5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Connectivity and gateways", "children": [{"id": "6c5c443a-4622-4b8b-8bf5-1c3f80f0d331", "type": "concept", "title": "Air, rail, road, sea, and multimodal access"}, {"id": "ecc952d4-dbc6-4f1c-bbd9-874691e41d54", "type": "concept", "title": "Routes, frequency, capacity, visas, and border processes"}, {"id": "04166cd8-fe58-4816-b56c-4743b6ca28b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Gateway cities, hubs, terminals, and transfers"}, {"id": "306ef7ef-74db-446f-98a9-a044f683d538", "type": "concept", "title": "Market access, reliability, affordability, and equity"}], "description": "Origin access and gateway performance determine who can visit, at what cost, and with what emissions."}, {"id": "8f61928d-c1f8-40e8-8d33-cc465f142657", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Destination mobility", "children": [{"id": "696d9863-dca7-4591-a9b1-f68865e91e37", "type": "concept", "title": "Public transport, walking, cycling, shuttles, taxis, and rentals"}, {"id": "9f7c4fe8-e43b-44a5-9e60-2639bc7ca195", "type": "concept", "title": "Parking, curb space, wayfinding, and micromobility"}, {"id": "0c31cccc-c50c-460f-9f6e-462a00ff5616", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal design and accessible tourism"}, {"id": "a83dd619-2a35-4cd1-a1c1-2eff0318fd37", "type": "concept", "title": "Integrated tickets, mobility-as-a-service, and demand management"}], "description": "Last-mile movement shapes congestion, visitor experience, resident access, and environmental impact."}, {"id": "68421f6c-3905-4a58-973e-c8278f47de1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visitor-flow analysis", "children": [{"id": "40905b8d-6139-4f7b-a08e-857c44362449", "type": "concept", "title": "Origins, destinations, paths, dwell time, and bottlenecks"}, {"id": "b71709e8-bed0-479d-b7ff-84bdb017eebf", "type": "concept", "title": "Peak spreading and timed arrival"}, {"id": "f71992ea-923f-47f0-b8a0-f34b2502f172", "type": "concept", "title": "Itinerary design, dispersal, and secondary sites"}, {"id": "ebb0bbb8-9695-4a68-ba58-b9d566f507ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Emissions, safety, resident mobility, and monitoring"}], "description": "Flow data helps distribute visitors across space and time without simply exporting pressure elsewhere."}]}, {"id": "ed60a729-631f-4701-a442-41a88fdedcb4", "type": "topic", "title": "Policy, Governance, Institutions, and Regulation", "description": "Examines how mandates, jurisdiction, public-private coordination, land-use rules, taxation, licensing, labor, and enforcement shape destination outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "5d40acde-890d-4899-a4ae-570e36367cb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multilevel governance", "children": [{"id": "dc25e14c-a140-4cce-bb5d-2b64cf27b924", "type": "concept", "title": "National, regional, local, and site-level roles"}, {"id": "3079687f-f2e2-4abb-bc5d-ce632f456f1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Horizontal and vertical coordination"}, {"id": "11189301-4ec3-40ad-bc3d-a5f5c0166b0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Public-private-community partnerships"}, {"id": "90dedb8f-5137-4d67-8a27-dbcf988ce054", "type": "concept", "title": "Interagency agreements and destination boundaries"}], "description": "Tourism crosses administrative boundaries and requires coordination among institutions with different mandates."}, {"id": "bb8d4479-2cdd-419f-a0e0-3e8577cd52f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy instruments", "children": [{"id": "d152f89b-36b3-4b10-98fa-c5fbeb93df92", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategies, standards, permits, licenses, and quotas"}, {"id": "ff397a19-ed9e-41ad-9776-89de61d87c99", "type": "concept", "title": "Taxes, levies, grants, subsidies, and pricing"}, {"id": "950b9c5e-ad6d-4b8b-bd77-ae8e6961deb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Public investment, procurement, and concessions"}, {"id": "52ad213e-eb61-4531-9e5f-51fa5714ed6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Education, nudges, voluntary codes, and certification"}], "description": "Plans become effective through a deliberate mix of information, incentives, investment, rules, and enforcement."}, {"id": "e69d3345-f652-4efb-8aa2-9518820cffb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions and accountability", "children": [{"id": "e5e12cdd-9baa-4d02-b476-3d90825038fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Mandates, capacity, budgets, and staffing"}, {"id": "f5f17fc9-e9ce-495b-a260-bffd40e1e3a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation and conflict of interest"}, {"id": "fb67ba56-d7b9-46b8-853d-73eb684df4a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency, open data, audits, and reporting"}, {"id": "94f4fe13-fc51-4d93-b4f7-8a8926a5b869", "type": "concept", "title": "Enforcement, grievance, appeal, and adaptive policy"}], "description": "Good governance requires legitimacy, capability, transparency, and remedies when commitments fail."}]}, {"id": "6516ef63-9b7a-4d45-acd4-05ef66d4db84", "type": "topic", "title": "Destination Economics, Investment, and Project Appraisal", "description": "Builds the financial and economic reasoning needed to compare projects, incentives, public value, leakage, local linkages, feasibility, and risk.", "children": [{"id": "a98fe28d-b0e2-4efc-9552-8afb247cea62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Destination economic structure", "children": [{"id": "3bc26d57-6cf8-4034-893b-548ec42f19ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Tourism satellite accounts and local value chains"}, {"id": "b5edf3b9-eab4-4771-a9d3-2a064a8a5ae2", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonality, labor, productivity, and enterprise structure"}, {"id": "d4193c72-e5da-4601-af31-e1c7b55c9df5", "type": "concept", "title": "Leakage, linkages, and import substitution"}, {"id": "b21408f5-e009-48b6-9187-b9fda9ae0fbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Fiscal revenues, public costs, and economic dependence"}], "description": "Planners need to see how visitor spending moves through businesses, households, government, and imports."}, {"id": "0ffb5746-03c6-444c-9436-275cff78271b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project feasibility", "children": [{"id": "b71e238b-d2b0-4b1d-835d-81f5ba4832ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand, occupancy, spend, price, and revenue assumptions"}, {"id": "814ab096-0bdd-405e-a720-2a777242c2e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital and operating costs"}, {"id": "ea1a26fe-7f6a-4365-81dd-2c54ed5b57c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Cash flow, break-even, sensitivity, and scenario analysis"}, {"id": "ddcdd156-8dbc-47ef-a692-f18f16a79142", "type": "concept", "title": "Market, construction, operating, climate, and policy risks"}], "description": "Commercial feasibility is necessary but not sufficient for a destination project."}, {"id": "c3036d5b-05ba-4e1f-b851-ac683892f686", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic and public-value appraisal", "children": [{"id": "d753f50d-d1f7-4f75-8984-546ea1f33718", "type": "concept", "title": "Financial versus economic appraisal"}, {"id": "92878ec6-317b-4a83-81a1-fd7e50ba560b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-benefit and cost-effectiveness concepts"}, {"id": "af9b4c34-8bbc-4af8-8842-9dd54311ff25", "type": "concept", "title": "Externalities, shadow values, and opportunity cost"}, {"id": "300f7298-5e55-4a6a-a1ef-e3311e71d912", "type": "concept", "title": "Incentives, additionality, safeguards, and benefit-sharing conditions"}], "description": "Public decisions should compare wider benefits, costs, distribution, and alternatives."}]}, {"id": "a515407f-284a-4912-a094-972c80e65a7a", "type": "topic", "title": "Visitor Management, Carrying Capacity, and Overtourism", "description": "Replaces a single carrying-capacity number with adaptive management of pressures, thresholds, behavior, dispersal, booking, pricing, and resident experience.", "children": [{"id": "31760073-35b9-4235-ae38-4ac19ad11de8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnosing pressure", "children": [{"id": "28684c94-05fe-4c00-8724-1d671cf9a2dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Crowding, congestion, housing, waste, noise, and ecological stress"}, {"id": "8185c9a8-d57e-453d-ae09-39235facdc47", "type": "concept", "title": "Resident sentiment and social license"}, {"id": "ed5bfc3c-3fb1-4825-bde5-c4c5f6cad1a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Spatial and temporal concentration"}, {"id": "c48fb4bf-327a-4aa1-b07d-9146b98e5cf7", "type": "concept", "title": "Drivers, thresholds, and early-warning indicators"}], "description": "Overtourism is a place-specific mismatch among volume, behavior, timing, infrastructure, governance, and community tolerance."}, {"id": "fdea07d2-eb14-4192-bea8-ed1945a7c2a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capacity and limits of acceptable change", "children": [{"id": "d03952a7-f5da-473d-a043-493621bbe6f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Physical, ecological, social, facility, and managerial capacity"}, {"id": "94f9ee76-5736-41e9-80d5-6498ab5d078e", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards and indicators of acceptable change"}, {"id": "23997dad-5bc8-4759-8411-61c267baa137", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoning, thresholds, triggers, and monitoring"}, {"id": "eda7065b-b76a-45e3-b0e9-bbd0fcf3d88e", "type": "concept", "title": "Uncertainty and adaptive management"}], "description": "A fixed maximum visitor number rarely captures different sites, seasons, behaviors, and management conditions."}, {"id": "1fc16eee-3054-42e8-86dd-36d48cf7ddf9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Management tools", "children": [{"id": "fe544214-f098-4733-9e82-bf36878dc6ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Reservations, permits, quotas, and timed entry"}, {"id": "c415f164-76df-4f62-8a67-060ea34799a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Pricing, levies, and differential fees"}, {"id": "34403872-d8ce-49dd-b8b1-036b62e29a20", "type": "concept", "title": "Dispersal, routes, real-time information, and site design"}, {"id": "d2641d8e-756f-4ead-b565-9fa9aee397c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Codes, guides, enforcement, closures, and evaluation"}], "description": "Effective visitor management combines access, information, price, design, and enforcement."}]}, {"id": "2f7e19d4-785f-42a0-a946-bc32acd15880", "type": "topic", "title": "Climate Risk, Crisis Preparedness, Recovery, and Transformation", "description": "Prepares destinations for climate hazards, health events, disasters, security incidents, and market shocks through prevention, continuity, recovery, and adaptation.", "children": [{"id": "388151b6-892a-4d14-a42d-018afe8c2218", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Climate mitigation and adaptation", "children": [{"id": "c2dfc9d5-bb48-430c-9a01-1a0053af7b9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Tourism emissions sources and inventories"}, {"id": "070e0126-a070-4d8f-8cf3-3528777bd7ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Heat, wildfire, flood, storm, drought, sea-level, and biodiversity risks"}, {"id": "7c72a15e-1174-4965-9733-97871119dac2", "type": "concept", "title": "Exposure, sensitivity, adaptive capacity, and vulnerability"}, {"id": "132fc448-651d-4461-bcd1-dc691c6ec27c", "type": "concept", "title": "Adaptation pathways, maladaptation, and climate justice"}], "description": "Destinations must reduce emissions while adapting assets, ecosystems, operations, and markets to changing hazards."}, {"id": "00541acb-6036-4c6a-a660-1545c7974da3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crisis preparedness and continuity", "children": [{"id": "1bbc2b59-07b4-4dc7-8ebf-3dc606627c9c", "type": "concept", "title": "All-hazards risk register and scenario planning"}, {"id": "b76f1c33-a81c-472e-8e25-f9ea930e9659", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident roles, coordination, evacuation, and visitor accountability"}, {"id": "37c3c343-8ef2-4263-a60c-75fa933fadd7", "type": "concept", "title": "Business continuity and supply-chain resilience"}, {"id": "774871a8-72b2-43c8-b73f-8d8d9de65171", "type": "concept", "title": "Accurate, accessible, and coordinated communication"}], "description": "Clear roles and rehearsed protocols reduce harm and confusion during fast-moving events."}, {"id": "9403e9dc-5e05-418e-8f8a-ec607fcedbca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recovery and transformation", "children": [{"id": "888bf6ac-8ed8-4381-b487-ac80115f2796", "type": "concept", "title": "Damage and needs assessment"}, {"id": "a8ef3897-5438-4b02-b05b-7e8e387d32cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Market recovery, worker/business support, and sequencing"}, {"id": "ce531b85-4b32-4b49-bd1b-a6f8776eeab1", "type": "concept", "title": "Reputation, transparency, and ethical messaging"}, {"id": "18556003-9928-4309-bcd3-ddd678970e4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Build-back-better criteria, diversification, and after-action learning"}], "description": "Recovery can rebuild prior vulnerability or create a safer, more diversified destination."}]}, {"id": "12dd8728-51c4-4cc6-8ccf-b23ea52485a5", "type": "topic", "title": "Destination Data, Smart Tourism, Indicators, and Evaluation", "description": "Creates an evidence system using visitor, resident, economic, spatial, environmental, and digital data while addressing governance, privacy, bias, and decision use.", "children": [{"id": "4660a62b-139b-478d-a587-25a301d1890e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Destination evidence system", "children": [{"id": "8a5265e7-9127-4890-985a-1487738d352f", "type": "concept", "title": "Visitor arrivals, nights, spend, origin, purpose, and satisfaction"}, {"id": "b67d3ac8-60c8-4078-a8ca-d2ea1534ce79", "type": "concept", "title": "Resident sentiment, labor, housing, and local business"}, {"id": "68d959ab-6663-45e4-985e-0ea22cbda6be", "type": "concept", "title": "Water, energy, waste, carbon, biodiversity, and congestion"}, {"id": "8393e6be-af99-4ae8-990a-e3f7bea1d85f", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative, survey, sensor, mobile, transaction, and geospatial data"}], "description": "A useful evidence system connects questions and decisions to reliable, proportionate data."}, {"id": "a99d3e74-8b14-474e-863e-663976b9be8a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Indicators and observatories", "children": [{"id": "10ab093c-8ce6-4602-8941-c0af4acecc43", "type": "concept", "title": "Economic, social, cultural, environmental, and governance KPIs"}, {"id": "472add93-6990-4459-be07-833f84f1361e", "type": "concept", "title": "Input, output, outcome, and impact measures"}, {"id": "bad04704-1aa9-46db-a763-d8772795a3a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Tourism observatories and data partnerships"}, {"id": "3cac20c4-63dd-4c8b-bd2f-c88da09908af", "type": "concept", "title": "Dashboards, disaggregation, metadata, and quality assurance"}], "description": "Indicators need baselines, definitions, owners, targets, frequency, and a response when performance changes."}, {"id": "a079e4cd-e284-47a9-8349-babc8ad34e06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Smart tourism and responsible data", "children": [{"id": "b6fbeb6c-2116-4f6b-a12e-fae7a068ba09", "type": "concept", "title": "Real-time flows, digital twins, apps, sensors, and AI use cases"}, {"id": "283e0812-3918-4b45-850d-cc2230d8b661", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, consent, security, bias, and accessibility"}, {"id": "a30960c6-cc6a-48ec-ab64-a55ef27a4350", "type": "concept", "title": "Interoperability, procurement, ownership, and retention"}, {"id": "4bc050b5-cfce-4427-bbc6-f7a3da15c1fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Pilot design, evaluation, human oversight, and public value"}], "description": "Digital tools can improve flow and service decisions but can also intensify surveillance, exclusion, and vendor dependence."}]}, {"id": "7a916127-7167-4b5b-b3e4-eb39651003ba", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrated Destination Development Plan and Implementation", "description": "Synthesizes diagnosis, vision, scenarios, spatial strategy, projects, governance, financing, indicators, and an actionable implementation roadmap.", "children": [{"id": "8cd9ae09-a8e9-4c7c-88d5-97a8f95f2061", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Vision, objectives, and strategy", "children": [{"id": "ef6f722c-8a15-4a11-8c71-08b18ded58c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline and problem definition"}, {"id": "e6a9a69e-f970-49c5-a66e-9a948b003e8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared vision, principles, and measurable objectives"}, {"id": "022beed1-4acc-4d55-bb82-14bfcded067c", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenarios, strategic options, and theory of change"}, {"id": "382eab7c-d8a0-4378-8aa0-0c408b457413", "type": "concept", "title": "Spatial, market, product, sustainability, and resilience strategies"}], "description": "The plan must translate evidence and participation into a coherent direction and explicit choices."}, {"id": "aa5173d0-19fd-4c10-baf5-ba17cb25b60e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Projects, financing, and delivery", "children": [{"id": "8faa83f6-b4d5-4ee4-a317-49761da48147", "type": "concept", "title": "Project pipeline and prioritization criteria"}, {"id": "2598f313-6a7e-4dc3-8a71-3f8b908e0d63", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept notes, sequencing, quick wins, and long-term investments"}, {"id": "bd9f5f3d-dfe8-4dc8-aac6-9bdff9de20f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Public, private, blended, grant, levy, and user-fee financing"}, {"id": "86ec1a0c-93cb-4571-a207-db2d98f24fa4", "type": "concept", "title": "Procurement, safeguards, capacity building, and partnership agreements"}], "description": "Implementation requires named actions, owners, resources, dependencies, and decision gates."}, {"id": "6f875f55-6348-416c-bec5-0e9816c304c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monitoring and adaptive implementation", "children": [{"id": "95e464e9-0a1c-414e-8e7a-a085f50c1a78", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation matrix, milestones, owners, and budget"}, {"id": "9daeda59-ebcc-4ee6-aaa8-a5fb2ae75dcb", "type": "concept", "title": "KPIs, baselines, targets, and reporting cadence"}, {"id": "af91d7a5-f08c-4d3c-b9f1-2860179fad4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk register, triggers, contingencies, and change control"}, {"id": "ae36a54c-1760-4089-ad97-6116c1c0aec2", "type": "concept", "title": "Public reporting, learning reviews, and plan refresh"}], "description": "A destination plan is a living governance system rather than a document placed on a shelf."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$tpdvjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'tourism-planning-and-development'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Tourism Planning and Development',
  goal = 'Tourism Planning and Development',
  summary = 'A Year 3 core course in evidence-based, participatory, sustainable, and implementable destination planning. Students move from tourism-system diagnosis through stakeholder engagement, spatial and infrastructure planning, sustainability, culture, mobility, governance, economics, visitor management, climate resilience, data, and an integrated destination development plan.',
  data = $tpdvjson${"slug": "tourism-planning-and-development", "title": "Tourism Planning and Development", "description": "A Year 3 core course in evidence-based, participatory, sustainable, and implementable destination planning. Students move from tourism-system diagnosis through stakeholder engagement, spatial and infrastructure planning, sustainability, culture, mobility, governance, economics, visitor management, climate resilience, data, and an integrated destination development plan.", "topics": [{"id": "d5052703-1ce2-470a-a857-fd46fd902959", "type": "topic", "title": "Tourism Systems, Demand Drivers, and Futures", "description": "Frames tourism as an interconnected visitor economy shaped by markets, hosts, firms, infrastructure, institutions, technology, shocks, and environmental limits.", "children": [{"id": "3f93a280-487b-4884-b733-620f3d880c20", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The destination as a system", "children": [{"id": "a62319d5-6acd-4a3c-8104-f0024631d0b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Origins, destinations, transit routes, and gateways"}, {"id": "e4ae8df6-2adf-44cf-a388-4f4a507a80cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Visitors, residents, firms, workers, governments, and civil society"}, {"id": "4de9dfbf-bccf-4a5d-a3fa-1f836d2d6958", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply chains, services, attractions, and enabling infrastructure"}, {"id": "3771b718-fe12-4d15-afb6-7a3892cc43b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback loops, externalities, dependencies, and system boundaries"}], "description": "Systems thinking reveals how visitor demand, businesses, residents, infrastructure, ecosystems, and policy interact."}, {"id": "01536eb1-be16-41f8-b4de-b4e6eac96a92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand and market drivers", "children": [{"id": "de7d0169-75cc-4725-b269-dddd5b0aacdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Income, demographics, exchange rates, visas, and connectivity"}, {"id": "a24a4512-9bc5-499b-9e5e-32c3d62c03cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Motivations, segments, source markets, and trip purpose"}, {"id": "91dbce0a-0de1-45ec-8133-2fecc1e472a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonality, length of stay, spend, and repeat visitation"}, {"id": "dc358168-3fca-455d-bb26-361e5769fc63", "type": "concept", "title": "Technology, media, geopolitics, and consumer values"}], "description": "Planning must distinguish durable demand drivers from short-lived enthusiasm."}, {"id": "ab316502-a27b-49b9-becd-097181950c9b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forecasting and scenarios", "children": [{"id": "4a00fe71-35ab-4622-88d6-d6d8b4747d31", "type": "concept", "title": "Trend extrapolation and judgmental forecasts"}, {"id": "53e64a10-743f-4745-bad5-9c11d21620d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline, high/low, and shock scenarios"}, {"id": "e6155643-65cb-43fc-b3f1-37f6077a9adc", "type": "concept", "title": "Weak signals and critical uncertainties"}, {"id": "ebd71029-bdcd-48fe-8e34-68c5be4699e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Robust, adaptive, and trigger-based strategies"}], "description": "Alternative futures prevent a plan from depending on a single fragile forecast."}]}, {"id": "483d956e-5a04-40ae-b41a-8496794194f2", "type": "topic", "title": "Destination Evolution, Competitiveness, and Strategic Position", "description": "Uses life-cycle and competitiveness models to diagnose a destination's position, path dependencies, product portfolio, and strategic choices.", "children": [{"id": "ea0ccfdd-1061-412f-af06-729dfa62e137", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Destination life cycle", "children": [{"id": "51c13206-4da7-4c61-8743-fa0892e41538", "type": "concept", "title": "Exploration, involvement, development, consolidation, and stagnation"}, {"id": "db659c6a-58eb-4759-8bb1-617925ea0d0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Decline, stabilization, or rejuvenation pathways"}, {"id": "f1f2775c-8591-4999-8b31-0e0b3b124b32", "type": "concept", "title": "Indicators of phase and turning points"}, {"id": "46b4a33c-07fe-4ca4-8918-ddcfaafb1237", "type": "concept", "title": "Model limitations and path dependence"}], "description": "Life-cycle models help diagnose development pressures without assuming every destination follows the same path."}, {"id": "f54518e9-4e37-4e0b-b147-855476fcfce3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Competitiveness and comparative advantage", "children": [{"id": "e0a138ad-8ab5-4291-8aca-a5eb80689fe8", "type": "concept", "title": "Core resources and attractors"}, {"id": "b431d957-1ebb-414e-967b-8b62d74a1f8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Supporting factors and enabling conditions"}, {"id": "963306cc-e5f8-4aa8-8a93-1e8fe5e312f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Destination management and policy"}, {"id": "cb87e54d-7bcf-4e0d-b0c8-e5d11253b62b", "type": "concept", "title": "Price, quality, accessibility, reputation, and resilience"}], "description": "Competitiveness depends on converting resources into valued experiences while sustaining place quality."}, {"id": "a5a954ea-fa7d-4eb6-8c24-e3ed08d5cce5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio and strategic position", "children": [{"id": "776e4426-9dcb-4ad7-b454-3cb0cba077ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Product-market matrix and visitor segments"}, {"id": "c0059bf4-3455-4da2-9179-f8c181b2f0a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonal and geographic diversification"}, {"id": "7eb277eb-7e86-49f2-817d-761df051c723", "type": "concept", "title": "Clusters, routes, events, and signature experiences"}, {"id": "9d4f4eaa-5388-4326-984e-80fcf47fde70", "type": "concept", "title": "SWOT/TOWS, benchmarking, and strategic choice"}], "description": "A destination needs a coherent mix of markets, places, seasons, and experiences."}]}, {"id": "5d862159-4c4e-4797-989c-6d712625738e", "type": "topic", "title": "Tourism Impacts, Resident Well-Being, and Distribution", "description": "Assesses economic, social, cultural, and environmental effects, with attention to who benefits, who bears costs, and how residents experience change.", "children": [{"id": "791b1a63-f247-4e3f-80df-3f3fda764412", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic impacts", "children": [{"id": "23bfd873-0f9c-42cd-9ad6-4ac35259a98d", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct, indirect, and induced effects"}, {"id": "ded8357a-31c7-4eb9-b0f1-075d1fea7f8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Employment quality, wages, entrepreneurship, and tax revenue"}, {"id": "c73dac01-423a-4581-855e-01f7a6d3dc64", "type": "concept", "title": "Leakage, imports, displacement, and opportunity cost"}, {"id": "6186fb4d-f9b2-444c-951a-7fede73ff2d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Local linkages, multipliers, and distribution"}], "description": "Headline spending matters less than the net local value retained and distributed."}, {"id": "6e214d94-c7dc-475b-b6e9-fdd418a864ac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social and cultural impacts", "children": [{"id": "01b86353-604f-41f0-a882-ab4797a1d8be", "type": "concept", "title": "Housing, cost of living, public space, and services"}, {"id": "3e698cc5-aeb0-424f-89f1-b2954343eae5", "type": "concept", "title": "Crowding, behavior, safety, and community cohesion"}, {"id": "0ed99348-857a-4f45-a9e4-c7521707bfde", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodification, cultural change, and revitalization"}, {"id": "1a722dc9-dd60-404d-aec5-f3a31e60bc8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Resident attitudes, social exchange, and quality of life"}], "description": "Tourism reshapes everyday life, identity, access, and power as well as visitor experiences."}, {"id": "14156f73-9c1f-45d0-913b-6d33c48da429", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Environmental impacts", "children": [{"id": "a8e52905-4690-4528-8d8f-991c2c5fb248", "type": "concept", "title": "Water, energy, land, waste, and emissions"}, {"id": "80306f55-657f-4eeb-84c4-bbe904235c49", "type": "concept", "title": "Biodiversity, habitat, landscape, and noise"}, {"id": "35400e0f-397d-4fdc-9186-f794f7e1e78c", "type": "concept", "title": "Cumulative, seasonal, and induced effects"}, {"id": "5ddbd7ba-4082-4f99-9ff4-28af482d2fbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental justice and ecosystem services"}], "description": "Destination quality depends on managing resource use and cumulative ecological pressure."}]}, {"id": "7e0a6481-c944-4504-91f7-59367aac1797", "type": "topic", "title": "Community Participation, Stakeholders, and Social License", "description": "Builds legitimate planning processes through stakeholder mapping, inclusive engagement, conflict navigation, co-design, and accountable feedback.", "children": [{"id": "201d1a89-6957-4805-9af6-3cb171cc4d4c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stakeholder and power mapping", "children": [{"id": "9356ed89-2f22-4e6a-8d9f-3b6113083855", "type": "concept", "title": "Public, private, community, Indigenous, and civil-society actors"}, {"id": "884577c0-7049-47b9-9928-037795011a91", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest-influence and network maps"}, {"id": "460a1b7e-5b66-4ce0-bb32-e931e390f1a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Rights holders versus stakeholders"}, {"id": "4bdea01e-47b6-442c-8556-bb08b6ae8d0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Power asymmetry, gatekeepers, and missing voices"}], "description": "Participation is meaningful only when planners understand interests, influence, rights, and under-representation."}, {"id": "4039beff-cb36-4eef-ac83-a0eefcb5a598", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Engagement and co-design", "children": [{"id": "0ce6a9d6-8057-4cbb-94a4-c9a9a9a56e5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Information, consultation, involvement, collaboration, and empowerment"}, {"id": "fb0bb080-afe5-4e7e-86f0-9578e96f4907", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviews, workshops, charrettes, surveys, and deliberative forums"}, {"id": "b2864132-81df-4a20-aeb3-107592c1febc", "type": "concept", "title": "Language, access, compensation, timing, and digital inclusion"}, {"id": "485f9a1d-a77b-4ade-90d1-ae5f70c1ac2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Participatory visioning, mapping, and priority setting"}], "description": "Different planning decisions require different levels and methods of participation."}, {"id": "97e889aa-0ee8-4003-9092-f58f647a142d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict, trust, and accountability", "children": [{"id": "1316c82c-35b3-4722-9548-33f2e7bad605", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue framing and conflict diagnosis"}, {"id": "3b98b8bd-c619-44c1-aa13-8293d410a212", "type": "concept", "title": "Negotiation, mediation, and consensus limits"}, {"id": "d77be00c-a6e6-4037-aeea-1c4ee13045ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Grievance and appeal mechanisms"}, {"id": "76efad33-59f5-4d58-98ad-839acb50c41c", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision logs, feedback reports, and ongoing stewardship"}], "description": "Social license grows through transparent choices, visible tradeoffs, and credible response to feedback."}]}, {"id": "a3e01fe9-4e07-42f3-9e54-06c6a2be06d9", "type": "topic", "title": "Spatial Planning, Land Use, Infrastructure, and GIS", "description": "Connects tourism strategy to place through zoning, site selection, infrastructure capacity, environmental constraints, accessibility, mapping, and cumulative effects.", "children": [{"id": "bce84e78-35c9-4242-8b7d-0c18b963157a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory and spatial diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "6bf8b87c-fbe5-49bd-a65b-b7d131e7b06f", "type": "concept", "title": "Attractions, services, accommodation, communities, and infrastructure"}, {"id": "4fc744b0-655b-4d6b-af04-095d96c325c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitive ecosystems, hazards, heritage, and protected areas"}, {"id": "cc51be7e-1590-426f-ba94-f85cdf0647ce", "type": "concept", "title": "GIS layers, field audits, and participatory mapping"}, {"id": "713e54b6-bcf2-4f1f-b29b-3e6b31dbcc58", "type": "concept", "title": "Hot spots, gaps, clusters, and corridors"}], "description": "Mapping makes assets, constraints, access, and uneven impacts visible."}, {"id": "382f1630-55a6-4031-ace8-05a03ff2d132", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Land use and site planning", "children": [{"id": "62feda3d-fc32-474f-aed7-aa68d6658f53", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoning, overlays, setbacks, density, and design controls"}, {"id": "dcb8c387-903c-490b-a65c-eac2361278cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Site suitability and alternatives analysis"}, {"id": "f641a692-f70a-42ea-a822-87441f9d1305", "type": "concept", "title": "Landscape, public realm, and sense of place"}, {"id": "0f384eb9-b71d-43ca-8111-37754f19c36f", "type": "concept", "title": "Cumulative effects and induced development"}], "description": "Tourism projects must fit place capacity, regulation, and community goals."}, {"id": "478595bc-0c9e-43f8-a914-8a22db181b18", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infrastructure and service capacity", "children": [{"id": "66edc316-5581-4ab8-92fb-c4f9240016f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Water, wastewater, solid waste, energy, and digital connectivity"}, {"id": "44a2fdf8-3bf4-4110-a508-8d31a6e06a07", "type": "concept", "title": "Health, safety, emergency, and public-space capacity"}, {"id": "353b91e9-423d-4798-9896-fe55d25b2c18", "type": "concept", "title": "Phasing, thresholds, and capital planning"}, {"id": "226fd8e2-4519-4d9c-b9b0-27b9cdc59ee9", "type": "concept", "title": "Operations, maintenance, and lifecycle costs"}], "description": "Visitor growth is viable only when utilities and public services can perform without displacing resident needs."}]}, {"id": "befc3ed1-43d5-40e5-93fe-2c07f87c1ba1", "type": "topic", "title": "Sustainable and Regenerative Tourism", "description": "Moves beyond minimizing harm toward measurable destination stewardship, local value creation, ecosystem restoration, resource efficiency, and long-term resilience.", "children": [{"id": "df4361a0-c5f9-416e-9e30-bcf6970f0d62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sustainability frameworks", "children": [{"id": "92488f3c-9f44-4f11-8246-192f51cfd7ee", "type": "concept", "title": "GSTC Destination Criteria"}, {"id": "28e2e26b-914b-4b8e-b008-31a09e2c0dcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Sustainable Development Goals and policy alignment"}, {"id": "652efe32-c242-4805-a110-3a920a122404", "type": "concept", "title": "Materiality, boundaries, baselines, and targets"}, {"id": "95048581-199a-4008-b8c9-fd263ec5303c", "type": "concept", "title": "Certification, assurance, and greenwashing risk"}], "description": "Standards turn broad aspirations into auditable management, socioeconomic, cultural, and environmental commitments."}, {"id": "2c51f8cd-0b62-4842-b7cd-8052d402966d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resource efficiency and circularity", "children": [{"id": "54209cce-988b-42d7-ba52-abd4403a489c", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy efficiency and renewable supply"}, {"id": "d9a7f5ba-5f92-4ef0-a89c-7795e23d797c", "type": "concept", "title": "Water stewardship and wastewater reuse"}, {"id": "55d32c2b-e421-4685-aec8-95b33a7bdab7", "type": "concept", "title": "Waste prevention, food systems, and circular procurement"}, {"id": "3087b681-5a9f-4b14-85f3-000032321827", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-carbon construction and operations"}], "description": "Destinations can reduce cost and pressure by redesigning material and energy flows."}, {"id": "0e8e7e36-7722-4910-b9bd-f94d22c74562", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regeneration and stewardship", "children": [{"id": "278edbf2-5129-4090-b6b4-e6009586618a", "type": "concept", "title": "Nature-positive and restoration projects"}, {"id": "1b3a40be-07b2-4c4c-ae9f-b238c72da544", "type": "concept", "title": "Community wealth and local ownership"}, {"id": "88b68518-00fa-41bf-a1b3-1374fb169614", "type": "concept", "title": "Visitor contribution and stewardship programs"}, {"id": "4791b831-6049-454d-8605-38f271fa2b3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits, tradeoffs, and evidence of net benefit"}], "description": "Regenerative approaches ask how tourism can improve ecological and community capacity rather than merely reduce damage."}]}, {"id": "e72dbd86-918c-44d6-a78c-196a816d3f73", "type": "topic", "title": "Cultural, Heritage, and Indigenous Tourism", "description": "Plans visitor experiences that protect living culture and heritage, respect rights and ownership, and avoid extractive or inauthentic development.", "children": [{"id": "356d9002-e7bd-4386-93b4-169840d172d4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Heritage values and significance", "children": [{"id": "141af013-dc82-437a-ac07-1c8adc286bfa", "type": "concept", "title": "Tangible, intangible, natural, and living heritage"}, {"id": "ba630f98-9cb0-4789-9037-783cd22f4b1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Significance, authenticity, integrity, and change"}, {"id": "c42103f1-8dd6-4141-9aab-a608b5e14571", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural landscapes and memory"}, {"id": "de26d3d8-4181-40e4-8da0-06fb807a6594", "type": "concept", "title": "Heritage inventories and vulnerability"}], "description": "Planning begins with what communities value, not only what can be packaged for visitors."}, {"id": "d339d287-ad2c-42dc-9f19-5b14f29a4900", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rights, ownership, and representation", "children": [{"id": "52e057a0-9c39-4921-b81b-896beb8b1dd1", "type": "concept", "title": "Free, prior, and informed consent concepts"}, {"id": "593749bf-4cae-43c0-a006-d5d5f192f395", "type": "concept", "title": "Intellectual and cultural property"}, {"id": "c7e7be21-3d46-4450-924a-6a965294813b", "type": "concept", "title": "Community-led interpretation and protocols"}, {"id": "e5289580-9107-46b1-8be7-c74616eb8477", "type": "concept", "title": "Revenue sharing, employment, and ownership"}], "description": "Communities and Indigenous peoples must control how culture, stories, images, knowledge, and sacred places are used."}, {"id": "a0cf4728-9087-41e6-a9a3-e88bfd7c6f25", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visitor and site management", "children": [{"id": "b4792930-8746-45d8-a0bd-90fcd2ad945d", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretive planning and truthful narratives"}, {"id": "82b446a3-dc6f-4767-b2c2-03e3b17254f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, zoning, routes, timing, and behavior"}, {"id": "59aca6fd-e077-49d0-bdc7-98f7fc62bd55", "type": "concept", "title": "Conservation financing and reinvestment"}, {"id": "fe83e36b-3214-4b4a-85a0-5ad86042b0f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk from commodification, crowding, and staged authenticity"}], "description": "Interpretation and access should enrich understanding while protecting values and daily life."}]}, {"id": "2ab6b507-1dbb-4e69-b64c-6eee6683adcf", "type": "topic", "title": "Destination Organizations, Place Strategy, and Product Development", "description": "Clarifies the evolving role of DMOs/DMMOs in governance, research, product development, visitor management, partnerships, and responsible place communication.", "children": [{"id": "ef0b4ca0-707b-42f1-9b8f-f8682cddad2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "DMO/DMMO mandate and governance", "children": [{"id": "314e19c3-784f-4588-8891-53aafe222227", "type": "concept", "title": "Legal form, membership, board, and accountability"}, {"id": "7526a552-7004-40a8-b020-3e5e7b3ca604", "type": "concept", "title": "Public funding, levies, partnerships, and conflicts"}, {"id": "1677cc91-9364-4841-a94e-7feca48cc948", "type": "concept", "title": "Research, product, marketing, and visitor services"}, {"id": "7c96f984-6489-4543-850d-d6704da2b56c", "type": "concept", "title": "Resident engagement and destination stewardship"}], "description": "Destination organizations increasingly manage and steward places, not simply promote them."}, {"id": "9c5ebb5c-0b92-4daa-88d8-af1702429dfb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Place strategy and brand", "children": [{"id": "46d12426-3f50-4569-aefa-ecaf3735d8df", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity, positioning, value proposition, and narrative"}, {"id": "770d74eb-990d-498f-920b-f1fac471d232", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand architecture and portfolio"}, {"id": "00f99349-aa55-4165-8d57-34d1c949c5fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Market fit and ethical representation"}, {"id": "2dfc557d-f883-4ec3-9e71-90366af76a72", "type": "concept", "title": "Reputation, crisis communication, and brand governance"}], "description": "A credible place promise must emerge from distinctive assets and resident values, then align experience and communication."}, {"id": "2d180bc5-68aa-4b95-a4f6-4b70c64a6e5a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experience and product development", "children": [{"id": "4a77cef0-b5f4-4d8c-a896-0c68e122f163", "type": "concept", "title": "Experience design and visitor journeys"}, {"id": "02693ded-3ea3-4362-b802-f442d8246d74", "type": "concept", "title": "Routes, clusters, events, and thematic products"}, {"id": "9a6b7a26-1f06-4e09-b154-51c6a5f1ee0b", "type": "concept", "title": "SME capability, packaging, distribution, and quality"}, {"id": "c19f941c-cdb4-417e-a786-fcb147a4965d", "type": "concept", "title": "Prototyping, season extension, and market testing"}], "description": "Products combine places, services, stories, people, and operations into bookable, accessible experiences."}]}, {"id": "0f1d0d80-6097-42b5-af42-22da0f36adcb", "type": "topic", "title": "Transportation, Access, Mobility, and Visitor Flows", "description": "Integrates gateways, last-mile access, mobility networks, universal design, congestion, emissions, seasonality, and visitor-flow management.", "children": [{"id": "2e4da67f-764a-4688-9acf-8f81e93efbe5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Connectivity and gateways", "children": [{"id": "6c5c443a-4622-4b8b-8bf5-1c3f80f0d331", "type": "concept", "title": "Air, rail, road, sea, and multimodal access"}, {"id": "ecc952d4-dbc6-4f1c-bbd9-874691e41d54", "type": "concept", "title": "Routes, frequency, capacity, visas, and border processes"}, {"id": "04166cd8-fe58-4816-b56c-4743b6ca28b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Gateway cities, hubs, terminals, and transfers"}, {"id": "306ef7ef-74db-446f-98a9-a044f683d538", "type": "concept", "title": "Market access, reliability, affordability, and equity"}], "description": "Origin access and gateway performance determine who can visit, at what cost, and with what emissions."}, {"id": "8f61928d-c1f8-40e8-8d33-cc465f142657", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Destination mobility", "children": [{"id": "696d9863-dca7-4591-a9b1-f68865e91e37", "type": "concept", "title": "Public transport, walking, cycling, shuttles, taxis, and rentals"}, {"id": "9f7c4fe8-e43b-44a5-9e60-2639bc7ca195", "type": "concept", "title": "Parking, curb space, wayfinding, and micromobility"}, {"id": "0c31cccc-c50c-460f-9f6e-462a00ff5616", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal design and accessible tourism"}, {"id": "a83dd619-2a35-4cd1-a1c1-2eff0318fd37", "type": "concept", "title": "Integrated tickets, mobility-as-a-service, and demand management"}], "description": "Last-mile movement shapes congestion, visitor experience, resident access, and environmental impact."}, {"id": "68421f6c-3905-4a58-973e-c8278f47de1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visitor-flow analysis", "children": [{"id": "40905b8d-6139-4f7b-a08e-857c44362449", "type": "concept", "title": "Origins, destinations, paths, dwell time, and bottlenecks"}, {"id": "b71709e8-bed0-479d-b7ff-84bdb017eebf", "type": "concept", "title": "Peak spreading and timed arrival"}, {"id": "f71992ea-923f-47f0-b8a0-f34b2502f172", "type": "concept", "title": "Itinerary design, dispersal, and secondary sites"}, {"id": "ebb0bbb8-9695-4a68-ba58-b9d566f507ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Emissions, safety, resident mobility, and monitoring"}], "description": "Flow data helps distribute visitors across space and time without simply exporting pressure elsewhere."}]}, {"id": "ed60a729-631f-4701-a442-41a88fdedcb4", "type": "topic", "title": "Policy, Governance, Institutions, and Regulation", "description": "Examines how mandates, jurisdiction, public-private coordination, land-use rules, taxation, licensing, labor, and enforcement shape destination outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "5d40acde-890d-4899-a4ae-570e36367cb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multilevel governance", "children": [{"id": "dc25e14c-a140-4cce-bb5d-2b64cf27b924", "type": "concept", "title": "National, regional, local, and site-level roles"}, {"id": "3079687f-f2e2-4abb-bc5d-ce632f456f1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Horizontal and vertical coordination"}, {"id": "11189301-4ec3-40ad-bc3d-a5f5c0166b0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Public-private-community partnerships"}, {"id": "90dedb8f-5137-4d67-8a27-dbcf988ce054", "type": "concept", "title": "Interagency agreements and destination boundaries"}], "description": "Tourism crosses administrative boundaries and requires coordination among institutions with different mandates."}, {"id": "bb8d4479-2cdd-419f-a0e0-3e8577cd52f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy instruments", "children": [{"id": "d152f89b-36b3-4b10-98fa-c5fbeb93df92", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategies, standards, permits, licenses, and quotas"}, {"id": "ff397a19-ed9e-41ad-9776-89de61d87c99", "type": "concept", "title": "Taxes, levies, grants, subsidies, and pricing"}, {"id": "950b9c5e-ad6d-4b8b-bd77-ae8e6961deb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Public investment, procurement, and concessions"}, {"id": "52ad213e-eb61-4531-9e5f-51fa5714ed6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Education, nudges, voluntary codes, and certification"}], "description": "Plans become effective through a deliberate mix of information, incentives, investment, rules, and enforcement."}, {"id": "e69d3345-f652-4efb-8aa2-9518820cffb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions and accountability", "children": [{"id": "e5e12cdd-9baa-4d02-b476-3d90825038fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Mandates, capacity, budgets, and staffing"}, {"id": "f5f17fc9-e9ce-495b-a260-bffd40e1e3a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation and conflict of interest"}, {"id": "fb67ba56-d7b9-46b8-853d-73eb684df4a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency, open data, audits, and reporting"}, {"id": "94f4fe13-fc51-4d93-b4f7-8a8926a5b869", "type": "concept", "title": "Enforcement, grievance, appeal, and adaptive policy"}], "description": "Good governance requires legitimacy, capability, transparency, and remedies when commitments fail."}]}, {"id": "6516ef63-9b7a-4d45-acd4-05ef66d4db84", "type": "topic", "title": "Destination Economics, Investment, and Project Appraisal", "description": "Builds the financial and economic reasoning needed to compare projects, incentives, public value, leakage, local linkages, feasibility, and risk.", "children": [{"id": "a98fe28d-b0e2-4efc-9552-8afb247cea62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Destination economic structure", "children": [{"id": "3bc26d57-6cf8-4034-893b-548ec42f19ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Tourism satellite accounts and local value chains"}, {"id": "b5edf3b9-eab4-4771-a9d3-2a064a8a5ae2", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonality, labor, productivity, and enterprise structure"}, {"id": "d4193c72-e5da-4601-af31-e1c7b55c9df5", "type": "concept", "title": "Leakage, linkages, and import substitution"}, {"id": "b21408f5-e009-48b6-9187-b9fda9ae0fbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Fiscal revenues, public costs, and economic dependence"}], "description": "Planners need to see how visitor spending moves through businesses, households, government, and imports."}, {"id": "0ffb5746-03c6-444c-9436-275cff78271b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project feasibility", "children": [{"id": "b71e238b-d2b0-4b1d-835d-81f5ba4832ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand, occupancy, spend, price, and revenue assumptions"}, {"id": "814ab096-0bdd-405e-a720-2a777242c2e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital and operating costs"}, {"id": "ea1a26fe-7f6a-4365-81dd-2c54ed5b57c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Cash flow, break-even, sensitivity, and scenario analysis"}, {"id": "ddcdd156-8dbc-47ef-a692-f18f16a79142", "type": "concept", "title": "Market, construction, operating, climate, and policy risks"}], "description": "Commercial feasibility is necessary but not sufficient for a destination project."}, {"id": "c3036d5b-05ba-4e1f-b851-ac683892f686", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic and public-value appraisal", "children": [{"id": "d753f50d-d1f7-4f75-8984-546ea1f33718", "type": "concept", "title": "Financial versus economic appraisal"}, {"id": "92878ec6-317b-4a83-81a1-fd7e50ba560b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-benefit and cost-effectiveness concepts"}, {"id": "af9b4c34-8bbc-4af8-8842-9dd54311ff25", "type": "concept", "title": "Externalities, shadow values, and opportunity cost"}, {"id": "300f7298-5e55-4a6a-a1ef-e3311e71d912", "type": "concept", "title": "Incentives, additionality, safeguards, and benefit-sharing conditions"}], "description": "Public decisions should compare wider benefits, costs, distribution, and alternatives."}]}, {"id": "a515407f-284a-4912-a094-972c80e65a7a", "type": "topic", "title": "Visitor Management, Carrying Capacity, and Overtourism", "description": "Replaces a single carrying-capacity number with adaptive management of pressures, thresholds, behavior, dispersal, booking, pricing, and resident experience.", "children": [{"id": "31760073-35b9-4235-ae38-4ac19ad11de8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnosing pressure", "children": [{"id": "28684c94-05fe-4c00-8724-1d671cf9a2dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Crowding, congestion, housing, waste, noise, and ecological stress"}, {"id": "8185c9a8-d57e-453d-ae09-39235facdc47", "type": "concept", "title": "Resident sentiment and social license"}, {"id": "ed5bfc3c-3fb1-4825-bde5-c4c5f6cad1a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Spatial and temporal concentration"}, {"id": "c48fb4bf-327a-4aa1-b07d-9146b98e5cf7", "type": "concept", "title": "Drivers, thresholds, and early-warning indicators"}], "description": "Overtourism is a place-specific mismatch among volume, behavior, timing, infrastructure, governance, and community tolerance."}, {"id": "fdea07d2-eb14-4192-bea8-ed1945a7c2a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capacity and limits of acceptable change", "children": [{"id": "d03952a7-f5da-473d-a043-493621bbe6f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Physical, ecological, social, facility, and managerial capacity"}, {"id": "94f9ee76-5736-41e9-80d5-6498ab5d078e", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards and indicators of acceptable change"}, {"id": "23997dad-5bc8-4759-8411-61c267baa137", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoning, thresholds, triggers, and monitoring"}, {"id": "eda7065b-b76a-45e3-b0e9-bbd0fcf3d88e", "type": "concept", "title": "Uncertainty and adaptive management"}], "description": "A fixed maximum visitor number rarely captures different sites, seasons, behaviors, and management conditions."}, {"id": "1fc16eee-3054-42e8-86dd-36d48cf7ddf9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Management tools", "children": [{"id": "fe544214-f098-4733-9e82-bf36878dc6ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Reservations, permits, quotas, and timed entry"}, {"id": "c415f164-76df-4f62-8a67-060ea34799a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Pricing, levies, and differential fees"}, {"id": "34403872-d8ce-49dd-b8b1-036b62e29a20", "type": "concept", "title": "Dispersal, routes, real-time information, and site design"}, {"id": "d2641d8e-756f-4ead-b565-9fa9aee397c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Codes, guides, enforcement, closures, and evaluation"}], "description": "Effective visitor management combines access, information, price, design, and enforcement."}]}, {"id": "2f7e19d4-785f-42a0-a946-bc32acd15880", "type": "topic", "title": "Climate Risk, Crisis Preparedness, Recovery, and Transformation", "description": "Prepares destinations for climate hazards, health events, disasters, security incidents, and market shocks through prevention, continuity, recovery, and adaptation.", "children": [{"id": "388151b6-892a-4d14-a42d-018afe8c2218", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Climate mitigation and adaptation", "children": [{"id": "c2dfc9d5-bb48-430c-9a01-1a0053af7b9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Tourism emissions sources and inventories"}, {"id": "070e0126-a070-4d8f-8cf3-3528777bd7ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Heat, wildfire, flood, storm, drought, sea-level, and biodiversity risks"}, {"id": "7c72a15e-1174-4965-9733-97871119dac2", "type": "concept", "title": "Exposure, sensitivity, adaptive capacity, and vulnerability"}, {"id": "132fc448-651d-4461-bcd1-dc691c6ec27c", "type": "concept", "title": "Adaptation pathways, maladaptation, and climate justice"}], "description": "Destinations must reduce emissions while adapting assets, ecosystems, operations, and markets to changing hazards."}, {"id": "00541acb-6036-4c6a-a660-1545c7974da3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crisis preparedness and continuity", "children": [{"id": "1bbc2b59-07b4-4dc7-8ebf-3dc606627c9c", "type": "concept", "title": "All-hazards risk register and scenario planning"}, {"id": "b76f1c33-a81c-472e-8e25-f9ea930e9659", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident roles, coordination, evacuation, and visitor accountability"}, {"id": "37c3c343-8ef2-4263-a60c-75fa933fadd7", "type": "concept", "title": "Business continuity and supply-chain resilience"}, {"id": "774871a8-72b2-43c8-b73f-8d8d9de65171", "type": "concept", "title": "Accurate, accessible, and coordinated communication"}], "description": "Clear roles and rehearsed protocols reduce harm and confusion during fast-moving events."}, {"id": "9403e9dc-5e05-418e-8f8a-ec607fcedbca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recovery and transformation", "children": [{"id": "888bf6ac-8ed8-4381-b487-ac80115f2796", "type": "concept", "title": "Damage and needs assessment"}, {"id": "a8ef3897-5438-4b02-b05b-7e8e387d32cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Market recovery, worker/business support, and sequencing"}, {"id": "ce531b85-4b32-4b49-bd1b-a6f8776eeab1", "type": "concept", "title": "Reputation, transparency, and ethical messaging"}, {"id": "18556003-9928-4309-bcd3-ddd678970e4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Build-back-better criteria, diversification, and after-action learning"}], "description": "Recovery can rebuild prior vulnerability or create a safer, more diversified destination."}]}, {"id": "12dd8728-51c4-4cc6-8ccf-b23ea52485a5", "type": "topic", "title": "Destination Data, Smart Tourism, Indicators, and Evaluation", "description": "Creates an evidence system using visitor, resident, economic, spatial, environmental, and digital data while addressing governance, privacy, bias, and decision use.", "children": [{"id": "4660a62b-139b-478d-a587-25a301d1890e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Destination evidence system", "children": [{"id": "8a5265e7-9127-4890-985a-1487738d352f", "type": "concept", "title": "Visitor arrivals, nights, spend, origin, purpose, and satisfaction"}, {"id": "b67d3ac8-60c8-4078-a8ca-d2ea1534ce79", "type": "concept", "title": "Resident sentiment, labor, housing, and local business"}, {"id": "68d959ab-6663-45e4-985e-0ea22cbda6be", "type": "concept", "title": "Water, energy, waste, carbon, biodiversity, and congestion"}, {"id": "8393e6be-af99-4ae8-990a-e3f7bea1d85f", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative, survey, sensor, mobile, transaction, and geospatial data"}], "description": "A useful evidence system connects questions and decisions to reliable, proportionate data."}, {"id": "a99d3e74-8b14-474e-863e-663976b9be8a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Indicators and observatories", "children": [{"id": "10ab093c-8ce6-4602-8941-c0af4acecc43", "type": "concept", "title": "Economic, social, cultural, environmental, and governance KPIs"}, {"id": "472add93-6990-4459-be07-833f84f1361e", "type": "concept", "title": "Input, output, outcome, and impact measures"}, {"id": "bad04704-1aa9-46db-a763-d8772795a3a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Tourism observatories and data partnerships"}, {"id": "3cac20c4-63dd-4c8b-bd2f-c88da09908af", "type": "concept", "title": "Dashboards, disaggregation, metadata, and quality assurance"}], "description": "Indicators need baselines, definitions, owners, targets, frequency, and a response when performance changes."}, {"id": "a079e4cd-e284-47a9-8349-babc8ad34e06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Smart tourism and responsible data", "children": [{"id": "b6fbeb6c-2116-4f6b-a12e-fae7a068ba09", "type": "concept", "title": "Real-time flows, digital twins, apps, sensors, and AI use cases"}, {"id": "283e0812-3918-4b45-850d-cc2230d8b661", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, consent, security, bias, and accessibility"}, {"id": "a30960c6-cc6a-48ec-ab64-a55ef27a4350", "type": "concept", "title": "Interoperability, procurement, ownership, and retention"}, {"id": "4bc050b5-cfce-4427-bbc6-f7a3da15c1fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Pilot design, evaluation, human oversight, and public value"}], "description": "Digital tools can improve flow and service decisions but can also intensify surveillance, exclusion, and vendor dependence."}]}, {"id": "7a916127-7167-4b5b-b3e4-eb39651003ba", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrated Destination Development Plan and Implementation", "description": "Synthesizes diagnosis, vision, scenarios, spatial strategy, projects, governance, financing, indicators, and an actionable implementation roadmap.", "children": [{"id": "8cd9ae09-a8e9-4c7c-88d5-97a8f95f2061", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Vision, objectives, and strategy", "children": [{"id": "ef6f722c-8a15-4a11-8c71-08b18ded58c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline and problem definition"}, {"id": "e6a9a69e-f970-49c5-a66e-9a948b003e8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared vision, principles, and measurable objectives"}, {"id": "022beed1-4acc-4d55-bb82-14bfcded067c", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenarios, strategic options, and theory of change"}, {"id": "382eab7c-d8a0-4378-8aa0-0c408b457413", "type": "concept", "title": "Spatial, market, product, sustainability, and resilience strategies"}], "description": "The plan must translate evidence and participation into a coherent direction and explicit choices."}, {"id": "aa5173d0-19fd-4c10-baf5-ba17cb25b60e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Projects, financing, and delivery", "children": [{"id": "8faa83f6-b4d5-4ee4-a317-49761da48147", "type": "concept", "title": "Project pipeline and prioritization criteria"}, {"id": "2598f313-6a7e-4dc3-8a71-3f8b908e0d63", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept notes, sequencing, quick wins, and long-term investments"}, {"id": "bd9f5f3d-dfe8-4dc8-aac6-9bdff9de20f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Public, private, blended, grant, levy, and user-fee financing"}, {"id": "86ec1a0c-93cb-4571-a207-db2d98f24fa4", "type": "concept", "title": "Procurement, safeguards, capacity building, and partnership agreements"}], "description": "Implementation requires named actions, owners, resources, dependencies, and decision gates."}, {"id": "6f875f55-6348-416c-bec5-0e9816c304c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monitoring and adaptive implementation", "children": [{"id": "95e464e9-0a1c-414e-8e7a-a085f50c1a78", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation matrix, milestones, owners, and budget"}, {"id": "9daeda59-ebcc-4ee6-aaa8-a5fb2ae75dcb", "type": "concept", "title": "KPIs, baselines, targets, and reporting cadence"}, {"id": "af91d7a5-f08c-4d3c-b9f1-2860179fad4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk register, triggers, contingencies, and change control"}, {"id": "ae36a54c-1760-4089-ad97-6116c1c0aec2", "type": "concept", "title": "Public reporting, learning reviews, and plan refresh"}], "description": "A destination plan is a living governance system rather than a document placed on a shelf."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$tpdvjson$::jsonb,
  is_catalog = true,
